1
00:00:00,161 --> 00:00:02,499
Why does almost everyone buy the large popcorn

2
00:00:02,519 --> 00:00:03,816
Because of the medium

3
00:00:03,973 --> 00:00:04,979
Picture this

4
00:00:04,999 --> 00:00:05,710
Small

5
00:00:05,730 --> 00:00:07,231
is two hundred rupees

6
00:00:07,251 --> 00:00:08,917
Large is four fifty

7
00:00:08,937 --> 00:00:10,038
That's a big jump

8
00:00:10,058 --> 00:00:11,606
so most people pick small

9
00:00:11,626 --> 00:00:12,774
Now add a medium

10
00:00:12,794 --> 00:00:13,988
at four twenty

11
00:00:14,008 --> 00:00:17,054
Suddenly the large is just thirty rupees more

12
00:00:17,074 --> 00:00:18,547
and it feels like a steal

13
00:00:18,773 --> 00:00:20,640
The medium isn't there to be bought

14
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,632
It's there to make the large look cheap

15
00:00:22,652 --> 00:00:24,232
That's the decoy effect

16
00:00:24,437 --> 00:00:27,401
A professor tested this with magazine subscriptions

17
00:00:27,421 --> 00:00:29,901
Online only fifty nine dollars

18
00:00:29,921 --> 00:00:31,799
Print only one twenty five

19
00:00:31,819 --> 00:00:34,347
Print plus online also one twenty five

20
00:00:34,367 --> 00:00:35,998
Most people picked the combo

21
00:00:36,018 --> 00:00:38,415
Remove the useless print-only option

22
00:00:38,435 --> 00:00:40,451
and most switched to the cheap one

23
00:00:40,661 --> 00:00:42,009
Use it in your business

24
00:00:42,029 --> 00:00:44,804
Say your gym sells monthly for fifteen hundred

25
00:00:44,824 --> 00:00:46,655
and yearly for twelve thousand

26
00:00:46,675 --> 00:00:48,856
Add a six month plan at ten thousand

27
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:51,769
and yearly suddenly looks like the obvious deal

28
00:00:51,994 --> 00:00:54,175
Save this before you price your next offer
